    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes a stale test expectation. `TestTiedOutputHead::test_row_parallel_tied_head_is_refused[False/True]` in `tests/unit/v1/moe/test_autoep_autotp_sharded_attention.py` fails on master:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAssertionError: AutoTP sharded an output head whose weight is tied to the input embedding\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe test (added in #8670) expects AutoTP to refuse a row-parallel output head whose weight is tied to the input embedding. Since 3c6a5ca95 (\"[AutoTP] Support tied embeddings for row-parallel…\"), AutoTP supports this case: it replaces the embedding with a `HiddenParallelEmbedding` that shares the head's sharded weight. The two changes landed a day apart, so the expectation was already stale when #8670 merged.\r\n\r\nChange (test only, no runtime code modified):\r\n- Rename the test to `test_row_parallel_tied_head_keeps_the_tie`.\r\n- With and without `zero.Init`, check after `deepspeed.initialize` that the embedding is a `HiddenParallelEmbedding` and `lm_head.weight is embed_tokens.weight`.\r\n\r\nThe original concern of the test still holds: under `zero.Init` AutoTP gathers the partitioned head weight into a new parameter, and if the embedding kept the old one the two would train as separate copies. The identity check catches that. Numerical training parity of a tied row-parallel head is already covered by `TestTiedRowParallelOutputHeadTraining` in `tests/unit/v1/autotp/test_autotp_training.py`.\r\n\r\n## Related work\r\n\r\nNo open PR fixes this test. #8829 and #8848 both list these two failures as pre-existing and leave them unchanged. I searched open PRs touching `TestTiedOutputHead` and tied/vocab-parallel output heads.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd tests\r\npytest -p no:randomly \"unit/v1/moe/test_autoep_autotp_sharded_attention.py::TestTiedOutputHead\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Test | master `cc7b5125d` | This PR |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `TestTiedOutputHead[zero_init=False]` | failed (`AssertionError` above) | passed |\r\n| `TestTiedOutputHead[zero_init=True]` | failed (`AssertionError` above) | passed |\r\n\r\n`pre-commit run --files` on the changed file passes.\r\n\r\nHardware and software:\r\n- 4× Intel Arc Pro B70\r\n- Level Zero driver 1.15.39122 (compute runtime 26.27.39122.11)\r\n- torch 2.14.0.dev20260804+xpu, transformers 5.17.0\r\n\r\n## Compatibility matrix\r\n\r\nTest-only change; no numerics, performance or memory impact.\r\n\r\n| | Validated | Not validated |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| ZeRO | Stage 3, with and without `zero.Init` (as in the test) | Other stages (not exercised by this test) |\r\n| Precision | fp32 | |\r\n| Offload | | Not exercised |\r\n| Parallelism | AutoTP 2 × AutoEP 2 folding, world size 4 | |\r\n| Accelerator | XPU | CUDA (the test is skipped on CPU) |\r\n\r\n## AI assistance\r\n\r\nThis PR was developed with AI assistance (GitHub Copilot CLI). I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\r\n\r\ncc @pengdurice @0z5a @delock \r\n",
